  "id": "Compound::DB01241 - Disease::DOID:3393",
  "verbalization": "Gemfibrozil is implicated in the pathogenesis of Coronary Artery Disease through a complex network of interactions. The evidence suggests that Gemfibrozil may influence the immune system by causing an increase in Antinuclear Antibody levels, which is then mediated by Ramipril or Simvastatin. These latter agents are known to treat Coronary Artery Disease, indicating a potential indirect pathway where Gemfibrozil's effects on the immune system could contribute to the development of the condition. Additionally, Gemfibrozil is associated with Hepatocellular Carcinoma, which is also linked to Coronary Artery Disease through the use of Lovastatin, further supporting a broader role in cardiovascular health. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of considering both immune and lipid-regulating mechanisms in the context of Coronary Artery Disease.",
